      "blocks": {
        "heading_z4tFdA": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "<span style=\"text-decoration:underline\"><strong>What Are the Main Benefits and Applications of Using Vinyl Tapes?</strong></span>",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_zEjt9P": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Known for flexibility, durability, and strong surface contact, vinyl tapes are useful across many industrial and commercial applications. This type of adhesive tape conforms well to a wide range of substrates, making it practical for labeling, striping, marking, sealing, and safety identification.</p><p>Designed to resist abrasion, weather exposure, moisture, and everyday wear, vinyl tape can continue performing in demanding environments. Many facilities use it to mark safety hazards, create lane markings, identify work zones, and provide clear visual cues in areas where safety and organization matter.</p><p>Although black vinyl tape is common, many color options are available to support different applications. Color-coded vinyl tapes can help teams communicate warnings, directions, boundaries, and process information more clearly.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_z4tFdA",
        "text_zEjt9P"
      ],
