    "image_with_text_bn6zUr": {
      "type": "image-with-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_dPE46F": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "What Are the Key Benefits of Vinyl Tapes?",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_hQLH4U": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Many industries choose vinyl tapes because they are durable, easy to apply, and adaptable to different surfaces. Compared with paint, vinyl tape is often faster to install, easier to use, and capable of delivering long-lasting performance in areas that need clear markings.</p><p>Rubber adhesive allows vinyl tape to bond quickly on contact. This makes it especially useful for lane marking, floor striping, hazard identification, and other applications where speed and reliability are important.</p><p>Another major advantage is clean removal. Even with strong adhesive performance, many vinyl tapes can be removed without leaving sticky residue behind, which helps protect surfaces and simplify updates or replacements.</p><p>Additional benefits include:</p><p>• <strong>Long-lasting quality</strong><br/> Vinyl tape maintains its performance over time and offers a strong shelf life compared with many other materials.</p><p>• <strong>Moisture and vapor resistance</strong><br/> Its protective barrier helps reduce the impact of moisture, vapors, and environmental exposure.</p><p>• <strong>Chemical resistance</strong><br/> Vinyl tapes can resist many damaging substances, including corrosive chemicals, acids, alkalis, oils, bacteria, sunlight, aging, and water.</p><p>• <strong>Strong physical durability</strong><br/> Many vinyl tapes are resistant to impact, abrasion, rupture, and everyday wear.</p><p>• <strong>Writable surface options</strong><br/> Certain vinyl tapes can be written on, which makes them useful for labels, identification, and temporary instructions.</p><p>• <strong>Stretchable construction</strong><br/> Their flexibility allows them to conform to curved, uneven, or irregular surfaces.</p><p>• <strong>Printable and customizable design</strong><br/> Vinyl tapes can be printed, patterned, sized, and colored to match specific project or industry needs.</p>",
            "subtext_color": true
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_dPE46F",
