    "rich_text_jdnUgW": {
      "type": "rich-text",
      "blocks": {
        "heading_3BpF6A": {
          "type": "heading",
          "settings": {
            "heading": "Choosing the NADCO Way",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text_nMNPqD": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>NADCO offers vinyl tapes for applications that require clear labeling, durable striping, and dependable safety communication. These tapes can help make work environments more organized, safer, and easier to manage while supporting compliance with safety requirements.</p><p>Available options include vinyl tapes with ink-receptive coatings, making them easier to write on when labeling or identification is needed. NADCO also offers vinyl tapes that meet OSHA requirements and provide resistance to heat, corrosive substances, and bacteria.</p><p>Different colors can be used to communicate different meanings depending on the setting. Our team can help you choose the right color, pattern, size, and adhesive construction so employees, visitors, and operators can quickly understand the message being communicated.</p><p>For many projects, vinyl tape can replace slower materials such as paint. It provides a faster, cleaner, and highly durable solution for marking, labeling, and safety identification.</p><p>NADCO manufactures custom vinyl tapes for a wide range of industries. With options for color, pattern, size, printing, and adhesive performance, we can create a solution tailored to your application.</p><p>Contact NADCO today to discuss your vinyl tape needs and create a custom adhesive solution for your project.</p>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
            "text_line_limit": "none",
            "button_style": "btn--underline",
            "button_icon": "none"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "heading_3BpF6A",
        "text_nMNPqD"
